摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Session-aware sandbox escalation compatibility plugin for DeepSeek Harness/DSH第三方模型会话沙箱升级兼容插件","id":"gh:1335780030","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-sandbox-escalation-fix","slug":"HakureiMonika/dsh-sandbox-escalation-fix","topics":["deepseek-harness","deepseek-harness-plugin","deepseek-harness-plugins","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","sandbox-escalation"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Session-aware sandbox escalation compatibility plugin for DeepSeek Harness/DSH第三方模型会话沙箱升级兼容插件"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-sandbox-escalation-fix (DSH 0.1.6-alpha.2 supported, Win & Linux & macOS)"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> [!IMPORTANT]\n> This is an independent community plugin. It is not published, maintained, or endors"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ed by DeepSeek, and it does not modify DeepSeek Harness core packages."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> [!CAUTION]\n> DSH `0.1.6-alpha.2` has significantly mitigated the issue addressed by this plugin. I"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"n testing, a model may still fail its first tool call because of unsuitable sandbox-escalation argum"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"ents, but it will usually adjust those arguments after receiving the error and eventually complete t"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"he call successfully. Escalation schemas remain registry-global and are still not narrowed according"},{"id":"p5s5","text":" to each Session's current permissions, so the underlying cause has not been fully removed. However,"},{"id":"p5s6","text":" users who can tolerate a small number of retries and some additional token usage may now find the o"},{"id":"p5s7","text":"fficial behavior acceptable. **Users should try the official behavior first and install this plugin "},{"id":"p5s8","text":"only when the remaining retries, overhead, or instability are unacceptable.**\n>\n> **Given the curren"},{"id":"p5s9","text":"t effectiveness of the official improvements, this plugin may stop being maintained after the next o"},{"id":"p5s10","text":"fficial release. If you still need this plugin to be maintained at that time, please proactively ope"},{"id":"p5s11","text":"n an issue, and the developer will respond as soon as possible.**"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> Currently supported:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"> Latest supported DSH version: `0.1.6-alpha.2` (full list in Compatibility)"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"> Desktop version: `2.0.3`"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"> OS: `Windows` & `Linux`  & `macOS` (theoretically supported, not yet tested)\n>\n>  If there is any "},{"id":"p9s2","text":"platform that has not yet been adapted and needs compatibility, please submit an issue."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"> *If it's useful, please stars let more people can see it~ Thanks♪(･ω･)ﾉ*"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Contents"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- What It Does\n- The Problem It Solves\n- Before and After\n- Compatibility\n- Quick Start & Installati"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"on\n- Release ZIP installation\n- Install into the default Web Profile\n- Install into another Profile\n"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"- Build the Release ZIP\n- Command-line installation\n- Manual Windows Installation\n- Upgrade & Mainte"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"nance\n- Upgrade an existing installation\n- GitHub commit installation\n- Manual Web Profile installat"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"ion\n- Uninstall\n- Why This Plugin\n- Verification, Behavior, and Plugin Cooperation\n- Troubleshooting"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"\n- Contributors\n- Development\n- License"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## What It Does"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"This plugin makes DeepSeek Harness show the model **only the sandbox escalation options that the cur"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"rent session can actually use**."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"In an All Access session (`danger-full-access` + `never`), the stock DSH tools still advertise `sand"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"box_permissions` and `justification` on `bash`, `pwsh`, `write`, and `edit`. But in that state:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- the session is already at the highest sandbox mode, so no wider mode exists;\n- the approval policy"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" is `never`, so every escalation request is rejected."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"When a model fills in those parameters, the call fails before it runs. The model may then retry with"},{"id":"p18s2","text":" different values and get stuck in a loop."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"This plugin projects the model-visible tool schema per session, based on the live Sandbox Mode and A"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"pproval Policy. It also adds a minimal execution-time fallback: it handles redundant same-mode reque"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"sts and, under `workspace-write`, removes a false `danger-full-access` request only from `write` / `"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"edit` calls whose resolved filesystem boundary is inside the current workspace."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## The Problem It Solves"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- Models still see and send `sandbox_permissions` / `justification` in All Access sessions, so tools"},{"id":"p21s2","text":" fail before they run.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### Why It Happens"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"DSH tools expose static escalation fields when they are registered, while the modes that can actuall"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"y be requested depend on each session's current Sandbox Mode and Approval Policy. The original model"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"-visible schema is not projected from that live session state before the request is built, so a mode"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"l can receive escalation parameters that cannot succeed. Tool validation then rejects those requests"},{"id":"p23s5","text":" before execution, which can start a retry loop."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- Node.js `^22.19.0` or `>=24.0.0`\n- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` `0.1.0-rc.5`, `0.1.0-rc.6`, `0.1.0-rc.7`, "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"`0.1.0-rc.8`, `0.1.1-rc.1`, `0.1.1-rc.2`, `0.1.2-alpha.1`, `0.1.2-alpha.2`, `0.1.2-alpha.3`, `0.1.2-"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"alpha.4`, `0.1.2-alpha.5`, `0.1.2-rc.1`, `0.1.3-alpha.1`, `0.1.3-alpha.2`, `0.1.5-alpha.1`, `0.1.5-a"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"lpha.2`, `0.1.5-rc.1`, `0.1.5-rc.2`, `0.1.6-alpha.1`, or `0.1.6-alpha.2`\n- `@deepseek-ai/cordis` `^4"},{"id":"p25s5","text":".0.1`\n- Distribution: public npm Registry (package `dsh-sandbox-escalation-fix`; `latest` and `next`"},{"id":"p25s6","text":" point to the newest compatible release), GitHub Release ZIP, local `.tgz`, local directory, or a Gi"},{"id":"p25s7","text":"t commit\n- Operating systems: Windows (fully supported), Linux (verified on real Ubuntu 24.04), and "},{"id":"p25s8","text":"macOS (expected compatible — the plugin is pure JavaScript and the `.sh` scripts are POSIX — but not"},{"id":"p25s9","text":" yet tested on a real Mac). The plugin itself has no platform-specific code; actual sandbox enforcem"},{"id":"p25s10","text":"ent on Linux/macOS depends on the sandbox backends available to the DSH host (Linux: `bwrap` or a La"},{"id":"p25s11","text":"ndlock-enforcing kernel 5.13+; macOS: Seatbelt), probed at runtime by DSH itself. When no backend is"},{"id":"p25s12","text":" usable, DSH refuses to run the command rather than bypassing the sandbox. The plugin's permission p"},{"id":"p25s13","text":"rojection and argument normalization do not depend on any particular backend."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"The plugin checks the installed DSH package versions at startup. Mixed installations through `0.1.6-"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"alpha.2` and unknown DSH versions fail explicitly. An initially visible target with partial escalati"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"on fields or an incompatible output definition rejects that Agent's registration; a target that omit"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"s both escalation fields is accepted as already safe. During runtime, a Preset restriction or stable"},{"id":"p26s5","text":" provider removal makes the wrapper dormant, while an incompatible replacement is isolated to that A"},{"id":"p26s6","text":"gent and target tool and reported without terminating the Host process. A later compatible definitio"},{"id":"p26s7","text":"n is wrapped automatically."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Why This Plugin"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"### It won't modify or bypass DSH's security core"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"`approveEscalation()` keeps its strictly-wider check, approval flow, and one-shot authorization sema"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ntics. The plugin only projects the model-visible surface and performs the narrow execution-time nor"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"malization described above:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"- no removal of the strictly-wider check;\n- no auto-approval when `approval=never`;\n- no extra permi"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"ssions;\n- no changes to DSH installation or core packages."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
